In article <1ei49aINN9n@agate.berkeley.edu>, datta@durban.berkeley.edu (Ruchira Datta) writes:
>I was just starting up a Priestess (I hadn't even encountered any monsters
>yet), and I found a cursed tin.  I was curious as to whether "cursed" is
>synonymous with "rotten" when referring to tins, so I decided to eat the
>contents of the tin.  After the usual difficulty with opening it, I got
>
>It smells like kobolds.  Eat it? [yn]
>	(Naturally not.)
>You discard the open tin.
>
>Before I could make another move, a kobold appeared in a doorway next to
>me, and I got something like
>
>The kobold swings its long sword named Frost Brand - More -
>The kobold hits! - More -
>You die...
>
>Did this have anything to do with the cursed tin?  And how did a kobold
>on Dlvl 1 get Frost Brand?
>
>-- Ruchira

I don't think it had anything to do with the tin.  I think it was just
bad luck.  Incredibly bad luck.  Almost unbelievably bad luck.

There is a chance of finding an artifact like Frostbrand just lying
on the floor (quite a small chance).  I think this is probably what
happened.  It was lying on the ground, a kobold found it before you
did, and picked it up and used it.  I think that's the unluckiest 
death I've heard of in a long time.

If you'd managed to kill the kobold, you would have felt very lucky
at finding a great artifact on level 1.  But such is life in 
nethack.
